      "writtenOn": "2026-07-21T03:43:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the connection is initiated by the remote device, `btif_av_handle_both_peer` calls `FindOrCreatePeer()` with `peer_sep \u003d AVDT_TSEP_INVALID`. After the peer is created, we set the peer SEP to either `AVDT_TSEP_INVALID | AVDT_TSEP_SNK` or `AVDT_TSEP_INVALID | AVDT_TSEP_SRC`.\n\nOnly after the connection is successfully established and we handle `BTA_AV_OPEN_EVT` (at which point the remote SEP becomes a definite value) do we clear the `AVDT_TSEP_INVALID` bit and update `PeerSep` to the final value.\n\nTherefore, when `btif_a2dp_on_idle()` is called and the connection was initiated by the remote device, the peer SEP is still `AVDT_TSEP_INVALID | AVDT_TSEP_SNK` or `AVDT_TSEP_INVALID | AVDT_TSEP_SRC`. In this case, we cannot use the original condition as-is, so the new check is **not** redundant with the existing one.\n\nIf you think the current implementation is not concise enough, here are two alternative proposals. Please let me know which one you prefer:\n\n1. Change the newly added part to the following:\n```c\nif (btif_av_src_sink_coexist_enabled()) {\n  if ((btif_av_get_peer_sep(local_a2dp_type) \u0026 AVDT_TSEP_MASK) \u003d\u003d AVDT_TSEP_SNK) {\n    btif_a2dp_source_on_idle();\n  } else if ((btif_av_get_peer_sep(local_a2dp_type) \u0026 AVDT_TSEP_MASK) \u003d\u003d AVDT_TSEP_SRC) {\n    btif_a2dp_sink_on_idle();\n  }\n  return;\n}\n```\n\n2. Remove the newly added part, and modify the original condition as follows to also cover the “remote-initiated connection” case:\n```c\nif ((btif_av_get_peer_sep(local_a2dp_type) \u0026 AVDT_TSEP_MASK) \u003d\u003d AVDT_TSEP_SNK) {\n  btif_a2dp_source_on_idle();\n} else if ((btif_av_get_peer_sep(local_a2dp_type) \u0026 AVDT_TSEP_MASK) \u003d\u003d AVDT_TSEP_SRC) {\n  btif_a2dp_sink_on_idle();\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "5da7e77a_13d0265b",
